### 4.3 Design of Learning Services


#### 4.3.1 General

The top management shall design a learning service consisting of curriculum, learning materials and means of assessment and evaluation based on the following:

- a) Expected needs of the learner;
- b) Proposed intensity and duration of the course;
- c) Prerequisites for undertaking the course;
- d) Synchronous and asynchronous scheduling;
- e) Methods, resources, and responsibilities to optimize the effective transaction of curriculum and transfer of learning;
- f) Intended means of assessment;
- g) Intended procedure of monitoring and evaluation;
- h) Age group for which the course is applicable shall be specified as per existing regulatory requirement/guideline;
- j) Social and cultural needs, as well as the background of the learners; and
- k) Accessibility of uploaded content, e-resources and related materials with facility of digital search function.
The curriculum, learning resources, and the means of assessment and evaluation shall be disclosed to relevant stakeholders.


